    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "North and south",
     "texto": [
      "Portugal is divided into regions. The **Minho** (Minho) is in the north and is very green. The **Douro** is the valley of Port wine. The **Alentejo** is in the south, with wide plains. The **Algarve** is the more touristy south, with beaches and cliffs.",
      "To say where something is, use **no norte** (in the north), **no sul** (in the south), **no interior** (in the interior): **Fica no norte** (it's in the north)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Preposition with regions",
     "texto": [
      "With regions you say **no Minho**, **no Douro**, **no Alentejo**, **no Algarve**: **Vou ao Algarve** (I'm going to the Algarve). With countries or cities, it sometimes changes."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
